// [S-Entry]. A token that begins no declaration is reported, and reading
// resumes at the next declaration. An `extern fn` is one: it is read as the
// declaration without a body that it is, so it is held to what an `extern`
// is held to and asked for no body.
?
extern fn _foreign(value: UInt8) -> UInt8

